  "details": "A lot of cool things are only possible with custom server code, which requires untrusted URLs. I’m assuming the main reason is to prevent IP grabbing. If this is the case, I’m not sure if you know about this, but Discord has a “proxy” system that is extremely easy to use, which is used for activities. Basically, you set your server URL in the Discord developer dashboard, and then you can access it through a proxy at the URL [APPLICATION_ID].discordsays.com.\n\nAdding *.discordsays.com to the URL allow list would allow us to run custom server code for worlds, while also not being able to grab IPs (as it’s a proxy and it would just return the IP of Discord’s server).\n\nExample: https://cdn-public-service-prod03.ol.arparec.xyz/useruploads/1761675312738-Screen_Recording_2025-10-24_083721.mp4\n\n(I can't attach it directly for some reason)",
